WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.340
<b>Ordeal</b>

3
00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.180
She lied to us.

4
00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.220
She said it was okay
for us to pass through.

5
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.810
But when we did, they
accused us of illegal entry?

6
00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.390
That's flat out fraud!

7
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.000
Exactly.

8
00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.210
But then, even if we were
told we couldn't pass,

9
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.010
we would've just forced
our way through.

10
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.480
I mean, how was that little
old lady gonna stop us?

11
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.730
Shut up!

12
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.480
In any case, you're in
a great deal of trouble.

13
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.650
You're now second-degree
criminals, and as such,

14
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.330
I'm afraid Conis and I are
unable to assist you any longer.

15
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.380
Why are you talking to us
from way over there?

16
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.820
I don't really see
what the big deal is.

17
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.500
I'm surprised you're not
used to this by now.

18
00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.120
[chuckles]

19
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.120
[LUFFY]
I've been meaning to ask.

20
00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.090
Why'd you come back, Nami?

21
00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.180
What?

22
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.680
We were finally gonna
get to set sail

23
00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.090
and head out on an amazing
adventure until you...

24
00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.300
I mean, we were about
to come looking for you.

25
00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.440
We were getting worried.

26
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.690
[LUFFY chuckles]

27
00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:49.900
I think you and I need
to have a little talk.

28
00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.010
[yelps]

29
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.720
[NAMI]
Forget about your big adventure.

30
00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.640
It's never gonna happen.

31
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.200
You haven't seen what I've seen.

32
00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.940
That island is full
of the type of people

33
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.020
you don't wanna mess with.

34
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.860
I don't care who
you think you are.

35
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.530
Granted, we don't know
what this guy is,

36
00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.950
but his powers are real.

37
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.320
And there's no way I'm ever
goin' back there again.

38
00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.660
So forget it. Got me?

39
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.080
How 'bout you just relax
here while the rest of us go?

40
00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.330
We're wanted criminals!

41
00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:20.500
I'm not staying here a
minute longer, either.

42
00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.690
Are you nuts? Get your
priorities straight.

43
00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:25.360
The adventure is always
the most important part!

44
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.570
My priorities are life
first, then money.

45
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.560
Please tell me I'm
third on that list.

46
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.900
Don't push me.

47
00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.730
[USOPP]
You raise a good point.

48
00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.110
We put all of our energy into
just trying to get up here.

49
00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.310
But we never really
thought about

50
00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:39.980
how we were gonna get back.

51
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.660
[SUU]
Suu.

52
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.710
Is there a safe way back
to the Blue Sea World?

53
00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.040
Can we ever even go home again?

54
00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.590
There is a way,
but at this juncture,

55
00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.510
I'm afraid it's no longer safe.

56
00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:52.970
Your only hope for escape

57
00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.430
is to make your
way to Cloud End.

58
00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.100
From there you can travel home.

59
00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.510
What's Cloud End? And how are
we supposed to get there?

60
00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.860
[CONIS]
It's a region
that lies far to the east.

61
00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.280
The only way for
you to get there

62
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.780
is to travel across
the White White Sea.

63
00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.950
Okay!

64
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.120
So we sail east, and we
eventually get home!

65
00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.990
But I don't wanna go home.

66
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.060
Your other option is stay
and get sentenced to death.

67
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.150
Listen to me.

68
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.790
I don't want you causing
any more trouble

69
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.710
for Conis and her dad.

70
00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.960
No. Don't worry about us.

71
00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.340
Even if we leave right now,

72
00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.010
there's no guarantee we'll
make a clean escape.

73
00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.050
We don't have any time to
lose, so just get on the ship.

74
00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.720
You'll have your
adventure, I promise,

75
00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.430
but right now, we
need to get going.

76
00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.210
So come on everybody.
Let's set sail.

77
00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.490
[OTHERS grumbling]

78
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.940
Thanks for all your help!
We really appreciate it!

79
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.970
Ooh! Hold on.

80
00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.400
Come on! Now what?

81
00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.200
Hey, old man!

82
00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.890
Huh? What is it, Luffy?

83
00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.660
[LUFFY]
Can I ask I favor?

84
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.830
Ya mind if we take the
leftovers from earlier?

85
00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.580
Of course not.
They're all yours.

86
00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.540
Woohoo! Come on, Sanji!
Make us lunch!

87
00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.080
Glad you got priorities.

88
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.900
In that case, could I ask for
a teensy little favor, too?

89
00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.850
You're an engineer, right?

90
00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.310
I don't suppose you could
spare any parts or tools

91
00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.980
to fix our ship?

92
00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.720
What's mine is yours, Usopp.

93
00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.870
Feel free to take
anything you need.

94
00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.800
Uh, guys. Where are you going?

95
00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.040
[LUFFY]
Hello! They got food!

96
00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.170
Tell ya what, you go ahead
and ready the ship for departure

97
00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.720
and we'll be back
before you know it.

98
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:28.010
He's dead-set on goin'
to that island.

99
00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.380
Doesn't he get it?

100
00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.260
Don't take it out on us.
You know how he is.

101
00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.100
Seriously, try to relax.

102
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.810
Chopper. You're still on
my side, aren't you?

103
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.980
Aren't you?

104
00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.760
Don't answer that.

105
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.620
[CHOPPER]
Heavy point!

106
00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.870
I was about to drop the
ladder for you, you know?

107
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:57.210
[ZORO]
You know there's no
persuading Luffy of anything.

108
00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.190
He won't listen even if
we all gang up on him.

109
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.990
Fine, then I guess
I'll just stay put.

110
00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.820
Well, you're free to do
whatever you want.

111
00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.830
I know that.

112
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.110
But if I stay here,
I'll be killed!

113
00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.660
Yep. Quite a predicament.

114
00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.340
Jerk.

115
00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.630
Robin.

116
00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.680
Let's go beat some
sense into Luffy.

117
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.220
Won't work.

118
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.510
[sighs]

119
00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.810
I guess we'd have
a better chance

120
00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.720
against the White Berets.

121
00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.730
And you know they've
already gotta be gathering

122
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.110
reinforcements to follow us.

123
00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.130
[MCKINLEY chuckles]

124
00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.140
[MCKINLEY]
Follow you? Idiots.

125
00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.180
Eneru and his Priests
aren't going anywhere.

126
00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:46.130
Why should I bother when
your true judgment awaits?

127
00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.170
Once you weigh anchor,
your challenge will begin.

128
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.630
Your ship will set
its own course

129
00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.230
to the forbidden
Sacred Grounds.

130
00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.210
[MCKINLEY]
The Upper Yard!

131
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.280
[LUFFY]
This is really good.

132
00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:07.290
[SANJI]
Save some for the trip.
And for the rest of us.

133
00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.960
[LUFFY]
There's plenty here.
Why hold back?

134
00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.750
This does have
to feed all of us.

135
00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.440
Conis! Refill!

136
00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.440
Why don't you get it yourself?

137
00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.370
Speaking of, where is Conis?

138
00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.450
[PAGAYA]
I think she went to
bid farewell to the others.

139
00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.960
Oh, I brought you some more tea.

140
00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.950
[PAGAYA]
So you're the
shipwright for your vessel,

141
00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.130
aren't you?

142
00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:34.010
Well, not really.
Actually, I'm a sniper.

143
00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.670
[PAGAYA]
Wow. That sounds exciting.

144
00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.070
Yeah, I guess so.

145
00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:39.410
But it means we don't have a
regular shipwright in our crew.

146
00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.040
Let's see, how can I
put this delicately?

147
00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.420
I am cursed with supreme
skill on every subject

148
00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.460
and the whole crew relies on me!

149
00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.400
[laughing]

150
00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.900
[USOPP]
Yeah, it's a lotta work,

151
00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:54.690
but without me the ship
just wouldn't function.

152
00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.650
My official title
is Sharpshooter,

153
00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.950
but I'm also the co-captain.

154
00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:04.620
And that's why everyone
calls me Captain... Usopp

155
00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.040
[PAGAYA]
Ooh, your color arrangement

156
00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.330
clearly denotes the work
of a professional.

157
00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.540
Of course.

158
00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.460
I consider the plating
of food an art form.

159
00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.270
Naw, that doesn't work.

160
00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.820
Throws off the
whole arrangement.

161
00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.320
If I put the red one here

162
00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:20.200
and then the emerald green
broad beans across the back...

163
00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.660
Yeah. Ah, now this
looks delicious.

164
00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.410
I sure hope Nami and Robin
appreciate the hard work.

165
00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:28.660
Wow! It doesn't even
look like food.

166
00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.750
I've never seen such

167
00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.750
a beautifully prepared
lunch before.

168
00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.080
Here.

169
00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:34.960
I made one for you as well.

170
00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:37.650
Really? Custom made just for me?

171
00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:39.070
I've prepared all the food today

172
00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.940
according to a
theme I've chosen.

173
00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.220
I call it: "Love is a
Cruel Mistress Feast

174
00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.510
for a Fallen Angel."

175
00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.470
I see.

176
00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.640
I don't get what
all the fuss is.

177
00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.640
It's just a box lunch.

178
00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.830
How dare you trash my work!
You better watch your mouth!

179
00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.060
A great meal starts with
great presentation!

180
00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.560
[LUFFY]
Why bother?
It all comes out the same.

181
00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.440
[SANJI]
You're stuffing your
face without even looking!

182
00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:03.220
[LUFFY]
Yeah, and...?

183
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.380
Why're you so mad?
It still tastes good.

184
00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:08.220
'Cause food should please your
eyes as well as your palate!

185
00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.350
[LUFFY]
Well, that's just stupid.

186
00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.400
Not even I can eat with my eyes.

187
00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.910
[gasps]
Hey!

188
00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.280
Something's wrong with the ship.

189
00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.410
[SANJI]
Huh?

190
00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.830
What is it?

191
00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.960
Take a look! She just started
rockin' all of a sudden!

192
00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.150
Really?

193
00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.690
Hope they're not havin'
a party without us.

194
00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.150
Hey, look. It's Nami.

195
00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:35.090
Wait. Why in the world
is she wearing a t-shirt?

196
00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.680
I'm pretty sure we have more
pressing concerns right now!

197
00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.430
Guys, look! The ship
started moving.

198
00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.670
But why?

199
00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.840
They wouldn't just leave
us here, would they?

200
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.420
Whoa!

201
00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.480
I don't think I've ever seen a
ship sailing backwards before.

202
00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.190
But they haven't even
set the sails yet.

203
00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.480
Huh?

204
00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.730
There's something underneath!

205
00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:04.240
I think we're being
dragged away.

206
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.110
But by what?

207
00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.260
It must be...

208
00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.600
[PAGAYA]
It's the legendary
White White Sea

209
00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.810
Super-Express Lobster!

210
00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:21.010
Guys, we're being hijacked!
We'll have to abandon ship!

211
00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:24.300
C'mon, we've gotta move right
now! While we still have time!

212
00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.720
We can't leave the ship.

213
00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.930
Without it we won't be
able to get back home.

214
00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.850
Then I'll stay behind!
Just go now!

215
00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:34.650
Forget it! You can't defend
the whole ship by yourself!

216
00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.270
[ZORO]
I'll manage.

217
00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:54.850
All right. Makin' progress.

218
00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.260
[ROBIN]
I don't think
that'll get you anywhere.

219
00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.390
[ROBIN]
Come back on board.

220
00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:02.770
Why should I?

221
00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.230
[ROBIN]
You'll never be able
to significantly damage

222
00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.940
that creature, and we've got
bigger problems now. Look.

223
00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.310
What?

224
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.340
[ROBIN]
A school of vicious sky fish

225
00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.760
are following us
ready to attack.

226
00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.530
We can't jump ship
and escape now.

227
00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.990
Even if we manage to
defeat the sky fish,

228
00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:26.010
I'm sure that more will
arrive to take their place.

229
00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.370
Our punishment has
already begun.

230
00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.130
And there's no way to stop it.

231
00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.000
Heaven's Judgment.

232
00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.770
They must be taking us
to the forbidden island.

233
00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.670
Guess they got tired of waiting.

234
00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:39.400
Eneru's really got it in for us.

235
00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:43.860
Oh, no. Please.
I can't go back there.

236
00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.870
Luffy. Help us!

237
00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.120
Sanji, Usopp!

238
00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.180
Why, Nami? Why a t-shirt?

239
00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.800
You're still thinking of that?

240
00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.530
This is awful, Luffy!
What are we gonna do?

241
00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.160
We have to rescue
Nami and the others!

242
00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.290
[LUFFY]
Hmm.

243
00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.870
I wonder...
Where're they're going?

244
00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.960
Where're they're
going? Yes, right!

245
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.630
[LUFFY]
I got nothin'.

246
00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:28.170
[PAGAYA]
Um, well.

247
00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.760
[LUFFY, USOPP, SANJI]
– Huh?
– Huh?

248
00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.310
[PAGAYA]
Oh. Uh...

249
00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.100
The Super-Express Lobster
is a messenger of Eneru.

250
00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:39.150
He must be taking your friends
as a sacrificial offering.

251
00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:40.840
If that's the case,

252
00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.980
they are being taken to
the northeast Upper Yard.

253
00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.360
To the sacrificial altar.

254
00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.330
Say what?

255
00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.500
You don't mean that Nami
and Robin and the rest...

256
00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.530
The rest?

257
00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.250
...are gonna be sacrificed?

258
00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.350
To that wannabe God?

259
00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:55.840
That bastard!

260
00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:00.240
He better not harm a single hair
on my Nami's pretty head!

261
00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:01.680
[PAGAYA]
But listen carefully,

262
00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:04.770
because I have not yet told
you what else will happen.

263
00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:05.860
What? There's more?

264
00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:07.980
[PAGAYA]
You see, in Heaven's Judgment

265
00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.900
there are actually two different
types of criminal punishment

266
00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.950
and I've only told
you about the first.

267
00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.120
The second punishment
is a challenge.

268
00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:19.330
Your friends are currently
hostages in Eneru's hands.

269
00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:22.710
And they are being taken
to him even as we speak.

270
00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.870
Hostages?

271
00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.350
I'm afraid I must tell you,

272
00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:29.190
the criminals who are
to receive the judgement

273
00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:32.330
are the three of you
standing before me.

274
00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:35.070
Wait. What are you
trying to say?

275
00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.650
If we only had a map.

276
00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:41.070
[USOPP]
Uh. I know I've got one
of Skypiea with me somewhere.

277
00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:43.030
[PAGAYA]
Well, this one is very old,

278
00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.950
but it looks like the general
shape of the island

279
00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.870
is correctly rendered.

280
00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.250
[PAGAYA]
This is where we are now.

281
00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.670
The sacrificial altar where
your friends are headed

282
00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.220
is located a good distance
to the northeast,

283
00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.970
here in the Upper Yard.

284
00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.050
And I'm afraid there's only
one way to get there.

285
00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.100
[PAGAYA]
You have to take the Milky Road

286
00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.230
that leaves this island.

287
00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:07.060
And your only means
of transportation

288
00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.860
will be the waver.

289
00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.510
The road will take you
to a great forest

290
00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:14.360
where the Priests are
awaiting your arrival.

291
00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.450
Well, let's see.

292
00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.860
There's gotta be a better way
for us to get there unnoticed.

293
00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.400
If we just ride up
to the front gate,

294
00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.870
we won't stand a chance.

295
00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.130
Couldn't we sneak
around the side?

296
00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:29.920
Usopp's right.

297
00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.050
If we take the main road,

298
00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.470
they'll see us coming
and set a trap.

299
00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.590
That may be

300
00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.710
but even if you do
find your way ashore,

301
00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:40.340
there's no way that you'll ever
make it to the altar on foot.

302
00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:43.420
You see, your old map differs
from the current configuration

303
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:48.300
in that now the Milky Roads
criss-cross the entire island.

304
00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.000
The cloud canals you mentioned.

305
00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.160
Correct.

306
00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:52.500
There are hundreds
of them, of all sizes,

307
00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.960
running every which way.

308
00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:56.470
I don't think anyone really
knows where they all lead.

309
00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.060
[LUFFY]
Hmm. I see.

310
00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.810
That's why your only course
of action is as I've said.

311
00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.360
You must follow the main
Milky Road to the island,

312
00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:06.200
and from there continue
until you reach the altar.

313
00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.230
Is that so?

314
00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.230
And even if we do find
another way ashore,

315
00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.560
the canals will block us
from continuing inland.

316
00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.080
[PAGAYA]
That's right.

317
00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:17.150
Did I mention the man-eating
fish that prowl the canal?

318
00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:18.980
Geh. Man-eating fish?

319
00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.490
Sounds like they've
covered all their bases.

320
00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.920
So you're saying, if we want
our friends and ship back,

321
00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.780
we have to walk right up
to their front door

322
00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.410
and march on it.

323
00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.080
This is part of the
challenge you mentioned?

324
00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.910
Part of Heaven's Judgment?

325
00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:37.180
Yes.

326
00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:39.100
In Upper Yard, there are
four powerful Priests

327
00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.520
of unimaginable strength
who await you.

328
00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.690
[ringing]

329
00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.610
[LUFFY]
Hmm. Sounds like
a piece of cake.

330
00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:50.360
I mean, all we have to do
to get our friends back

331
00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.530
is beat up these Priests, right?

332
00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.370
You make it sound easy.

333
00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.080
[laughing]

334
00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.540
Finally, a little action!

335
00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:11.990
<b>Angel Beach</b>
<b>Lovely Street</b>

336
00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:11.990
<b>Upper Yard</b>

337
00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.260
[LUFFY]
Wow! This place is great!

338
00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:25.180
[CONIS]
Lovely Street is
the center of commerce

339
00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.140
on the Island.

340
00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:26.890
It has everything.

341
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.930
[LUFFY laughs]

342
00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.930
Check it out! Floating stores!

343
00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:33.980
[CONIS]
It takes a special
variety of island cloud

344
00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.310
to build those.

345
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:38.730
[LUFFY]
So where's all the
floating restaurants?

346
00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.710
Hey, guys. I notice everyone's
avoiding us. Again.

347
00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.180
[SANJI]
Can't say I blame 'em.

348
00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.590
Word's probably already gotten
out that we're criminals.

349
00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:58.550
So what else is new?

350
00:16:58.640 --> 00:16:59.930
[LUFFY laughs]

351
00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.890
[LUFFY]
Ah, let 'em be that way!

352
00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:05.480
That means we've got
downtown all to ourselves!

353
00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.690
All these gorgeous angels
and they're avoiding me.

354
00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.160
[LUFFY]
Huh.

355
00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.700
Sure is a lot of weird
stuff for sale here.

356
00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.370
[gasps]

357
00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.960
[LUFFY]
Aw, man. Too bad
I don't have any money.

358
00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:20.120
Hey, mister, do you
take treasure?

359
00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.510
Hey, Luffy, when you're
done foolin' around,

360
00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:25.640
there's still the matter of
rescuing Nami and the others.

361
00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.470
If you don't get
serious, and soon,

362
00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.600
they're gonna be sacrificed,
do you know that?

363
00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.900
[LUFFY]
You worry too much!
They're fine!

364
00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.820
Don't forget, Zoro's with them!

365
00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.810
Yeah, like we can really
count on that guy!

366
00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.040
I just hope the ship hasn't
sustained any more damage.

367
00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:41.090
I mean, she's had more than
her share of abuse lately.

368
00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:43.800
[LUFFY]
Huh. There's something
in the middle of the street!

369
00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:44.920
[CONIS]
Huh?

370
00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.350
[LUFFY]
What a weird face!

371
00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.220
What's it supposed
to be? A seal?

372
00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:55.060
[SANJI]
Looks like a figure
made outta mud.

373
00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.600
Knowing this place, I bet it's
some kinda religious statue.

374
00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.190
[USOPP]
Oh, you're both morons.

375
00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:01.070
This is art! I can tell!

376
00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.730
[CONIS]
This is "vearth."

377
00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.440
You might say it represents

378
00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:07.320
the eternal yearnings of
the people of the sky.

379
00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.320
Vearth, huh?

380
00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.570
Really?

381
00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.360
So what, you guys like,
pray to this thing?

382
00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:14.200
That's pretty crazy.

383
00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:16.510
[CONIS giggles]

384
00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.090
[CONIS]
Well, I guess it would
be difficult for someone

385
00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:20.970
from the Blue Sea to understand.

386
00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.340
Oh! We're almost to
the docks! Right this way!

387
00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:25.250
Aw! We're leavin' town already?

388
00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.340
[USOPP]
Already?

389
00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.760
We were never planning
on stopping here

390
00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:29.010
in the first place!

391
00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.470
[LUFFY]
I know, but I don't see why

392
00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.960
we couldn't stick around
a little bit longer.

393
00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.760
[ISLANDER L]
Phew! Looks like it worked.

394
00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.510
[ISLANDER M]
Yeah, they're
headed straight for the docks.

395
00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:41.970
[ISLANDER N]
We're saved!

396
00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.810
[chuckles]

397
00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.610
[LUFFY]
Look at all these boats!

398
00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.910
Yes, you'll notice
there are boats

399
00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.910
of all shapes and sizes
anchored in this harbor.

400
00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:12.160
If you look over here,
there are even more types.

401
00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.120
Whoa!

402
00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.790
That one! It's perfect!

403
00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:21.630
[LUFFY]
I always wanted a
gondola! We'll take it!

404
00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.180
Ooh! Look back there!

405
00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.890
I bet those dials make this baby
move quicker than lightning!

406
00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.550
This is gonna be
a whole lotta fun!

407
00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:29.260
Come on! Let's go for a spin!

408
00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.500
[SANJI]
You idiot.

409
00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.960
We've got to rescue the
crew first, remember?

410
00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.330
Get serious, will ya?

411
00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.540
[CONIS]
Actually, your boat
is right over here.

412
00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.130
[SANJI]
Great!

413
00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:38.920
[LUFFY]
Ooh! Ha!

414
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:40.830
Is it even awesomer
than the gondola?

415
00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.090
Oh, man, I can't wait to see it.

416
00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:55.220
Presenting: The Crow!

417
00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:59.480
Ah! You're kidding me, right?

418
00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:04.520
[SANJI]
Wait, uh, crows don't even swim.

419
00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:06.900
[CONIS]
I only learned
to ride a waver recently.

420
00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.060
Before then, I used the
Crow to get around.

421
00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:11.020
It's not as fast as
a waver of course,

422
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:14.360
but it has two Breath Dials,
and is quite reliable.

423
00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.320
Please, feel free to use it.

424
00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.530
Wait. I'm not going.

425
00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.620
[MCKINLEY]
Aha!

426
00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.540
I knew he'd finally
show his true colors.

427
00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:26.470
Unless I can take that.

428
00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.600
He's not scared; he's selfish.

429
00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:37.570
That one, huh?
You don't like the Crow?

430
00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.070
I'm sorry.

431
00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.860
The only thing sorry is this
guy! Apologize, you ingrate!

432
00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.520
She goes to the trouble
of getting us a boat

433
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:43.730
and all you do is complain!

434
00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.270
What's wrong with you?

435
00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.860
I'm sorry he doesn't appreciate
your help like I do, Conis.

436
00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.770
I'm sorry.

437
00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.800
[CONIS]
Your exit is Gate Number Two.

438
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:54.510
It leads right to
the Milky Road,

439
00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:58.100
and that will take you all
the way to Upper Yard.

440
00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:01.350
Just... Just follow it
and you'll be fine.

441
00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:05.870
[LUFFY]
Hey, Conis.

442
00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:07.000
Yes?

443
00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:09.730
You've been trembling
ever since we left.

444
00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.590
Is everything okay?

445
00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:16.350
Ugh. Can't hear.

446
00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:18.470
What're they talkin' about?

447
00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:22.080
[CONIS]
I-Is it that noticeable?

448
00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.560
Yeah. It's like you're
scared or something.

449
00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:32.020
No, wait. She wouldn't!

450
00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:33.200
[SANJI laughs]

451
00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:34.870
Don't you get it?
She's worried about us!

452
00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:38.870
Oh, Conis, that is so
sweet of you, my dear!

453
00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.710
[USOPP]
Speaking of being worried,

454
00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.050
are you and Pagaya
gonna be all right?

455
00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.510
I mean, everyone in town
is avoiding us like the plague,

456
00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.720
but you're leading us around,
lending us your boat,

457
00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.400
giving us directions.

458
00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:54.310
Is helping us gonna
get you in trouble?

459
00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:57.840
Doesn't that make you,
like, our accomplices?

460
00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:02.250
Conis, don't cry.
You'll gonna be fine, 'kay?

461
00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:06.290
You should've told us
you were scared.

462
00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:08.270
Really. We could have just
come here on our own.

463
00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:09.800
No, it's...

464
00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:11.390
It's not...

465
00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:14.380
[CONIS]
It's not what you think!

466
00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:18.820
She wouldn't dare.

467
00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:21.820
Don't say anything
you'll regret.

468
00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:25.100
Don't you get it?

469
00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.680
Even after I told you how
terrifying Upper Yard is,

470
00:22:27.770 --> 00:22:29.310
I still led you here.

471
00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:31.940
I even got you a boat and
told you which route to take.

472
00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.420
Don't you find that odd?

473
00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:36.050
Isn't it obvious
what's going on here?

474
00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:37.720
[growls]

475
00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:41.680
Watch your tongue, little girl!
Don't say anything foolish!

476
00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:43.890
[USOPP]
Huh? You hear somethin'?

477
00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:51.610
[USOPP]
Huh?

478
00:22:54.020 --> 00:22:56.860
[SANJI]
Don't tell me
they're all in on this.

479
00:22:58.780 --> 00:23:01.700
[PAGAYA]
Oh, Conis, please forgive me.

480
00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:03.950
But it's every citizen's duty.

481
00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:05.120
You know what will happen

482
00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:08.250
if we don't follow
almighty Eneru's will.

483
00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.090
[SANJI, USOPP gasp]

484
00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:18.670
[CONIS]
Just run away. Please.

485
00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:24.080
I'm so sorry, you guys!

486
00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:28.980
No, no, stop!

487
00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:30.990
What do you think you're doing?!

488
00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.530
I called the Super
Express Lobster.

489
00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:36.370
It was all my fault!

490
00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:39.340
You mean that thing that took
Nami and the others away?

491
00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:40.520
You called it, Conis?

492
00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:46.880
[CONIS]
While you three were
inside talking to my father,

493
00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:49.300
I went aboard and lied to
your friends about a current

494
00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:51.130
that leads to Cloud End.

495
00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:53.530
They believed me.
And I had them raise anchor.

496
00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:01.690
[CONIS]
That was the signal that
summoned almighty Eneru's

497
00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:03.830
Super Express Lobster.

498
00:24:12.850 --> 00:24:14.560
[MCKINLEY]
What? Do you want to die?

499
00:24:14.920 --> 00:24:16.710
You stupid girl!

500
00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:18.040
[CONIS]
Once we know
someone's a criminal,

501
00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:19.980
we must lead them to Upper Yard!

502
00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:23.420
If we don't, then
the penalty is death!

503
00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:26.760
[ISLANDER S]
You idiot!

504
00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:29.350
You're gonna bring his
wrath down upon us all!

505
00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:30.290
[ISLANDER R]
This is outrageous!

506
00:24:30.510 --> 00:24:32.370
[ISLANDER Q]
Somebody stop her!

507
00:24:32.370 --> 00:24:35.420
[CONIS]
It's our duty.
The duty of every citizen.

508
00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:36.830
That's crazy!

509
00:24:36.920 --> 00:24:38.460
[CONIS]
I know!

510
00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:43.130
I-I'm sorry. I should've
told you sooner.

511
00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:44.510
Wait a sec.

512
00:24:44.590 --> 00:24:48.550
You're saying they forced
you to lead us all here?

513
00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:53.020
If that's true...

514
00:24:55.560 --> 00:24:58.230
[ALL]
– ...then why even tell us at all?!
– ...then why even tell us at all?!

515
00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:04.630
[LUFFY]
Are you nuts?
Now your life is in danger!

516
00:25:04.630 --> 00:25:06.170
[ISLANDER M]
It's all over!

517
00:25:06.170 --> 00:25:07.530
[ISLANDER N]
We're too late!

518
00:25:07.530 --> 00:25:08.980
[ISLANDER S]
Get away from the girl!

519
00:25:08.990 --> 00:25:11.200
[ISLANDER J]
The judgment is coming!

520
00:25:40.730 --> 00:25:43.400
[yelling]

521
00:25:47.720 --> 00:25:48.990
It's too big!

522
00:26:24.380 --> 00:26:27.300
[USOPP coughing]

523
00:26:32.430 --> 00:26:36.310
[gasps]
What in the
world was that thing?

524
00:26:36.380 --> 00:26:38.670
It did that?

525
00:26:38.760 --> 00:26:39.590
[USOPP]
Luffy!

526
00:26:39.620 --> 00:26:41.500
[SANJI]
Conis! Where are you?

527
00:26:41.580 --> 00:26:43.080
Conis!

528
00:26:43.120 --> 00:26:45.490
Luffy! Conis!

529
00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:46.660
Hah!

530
00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:47.660
[ISLANDER W]
That's what happens to those

531
00:26:47.750 --> 00:26:50.330
who defy almighty Eneru!

532
00:26:54.130 --> 00:26:56.430
[GAN FALL]
Do not fear.
They are both safe.

533
00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:02.600
[PIERRE]
Pi-e!

534
00:27:02.660 --> 00:27:04.200
It's him! Gan Fall!

535
00:27:04.290 --> 00:27:05.330
[gasps]

536
00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:08.480
Oh! The weird old man!

537
00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:10.080
Me, "weird"? No.

538
00:27:10.080 --> 00:27:14.700
I am the Sky Knight, friend.
And this one's on the house.

539
00:27:18.590 --> 00:27:21.710
Conis! Look she's safe!

540
00:27:21.780 --> 00:27:24.030
[GAN FALL]
And she will
remain so under my watch.

541
00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:28.370
You have my word. I shant
allow Eneru to harm her.

542
00:27:28.470 --> 00:27:29.930
Thanks!

543
00:27:29.980 --> 00:27:34.860
Now that you've seen the scope
of Eneru's power and anger,

544
00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:37.110
what are you going to do next?

545
00:27:37.140 --> 00:27:40.390
The same thing we were
gonna do from the start.

546
00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:43.580
Go to Upper Yard and
rescue our friends.

547
00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:46.870
I see. May luck be with you.

548
00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:49.630
[PIERRE]
Pi-e!

549
00:27:56.440 --> 00:27:57.400
[CONIS]
What about them?

550
00:27:57.400 --> 00:27:59.660
[GAN FALL]
They have chosen
their own course.

551
00:28:00.100 --> 00:28:03.270
Do not blame yourself, child.

552
00:28:03.350 --> 00:28:06.940
I-I know who you really are.

553
00:28:07.020 --> 00:28:09.150
[GAN FALL]
Of course! It's no secret.

554
00:28:09.240 --> 00:28:10.320
I am the Sky Knight.

555
00:28:10.410 --> 00:28:13.370
No. We-We all know.

556
00:28:13.450 --> 00:28:17.160
Please come back to us... God.

557
00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:23.780
[USOPP]
Good luck, fellas!

558
00:28:23.890 --> 00:28:26.650
Hop aboard. Get comfy.
I'll give you good shove off!

559
00:28:26.730 --> 00:28:27.770
[SANJI]
Get on the boat!

560
00:28:27.860 --> 00:28:29.610
[USOPP]
I don't wanna!

561
00:28:32.870 --> 00:28:36.620
All right, Upper Yard,
here we come!

562
00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:38.950
[USOPP crying]

563
00:28:39.040 --> 00:28:41.120
[USOPP]
No!

564
00:28:44.170 --> 00:28:46.380
They-They went.

565
00:28:46.460 --> 00:28:49.420
Without any fear or hesitation!
